#!/usr/bin/env bash
# seq2cause-bench — m / latent / seed 4 — JOB T of the CONTEXT FAMILY (the test read), generated
# 2026-11-01 from freezes/2026-11-01-m-latent-s4-context.json (family context, 16 cells over both
# grains: the score × context 2 x 2 on the full-staircase core probe and the atomic CMI arm;
# model aa529274…, the landed seed-4 m backbone). plans/reference-arms.md, addendum
# 2026-10-31 (§5 protocol, §7 identity checks); D-SB-20 … 24. The test sample of plans/caps.md for m:
# 20k request / 10k session sequences, head order (as the landed m Job T).
# The provisioning replica of the same name (private infra/) runs `bash scripts/jobs/<this file>`
# from the harness directory; scripts/tfvars_check.py follows that segment and parses every
# `python -m seq2causebench.<cmd>` line below with the real parsers. One discover call per
# (grain, probe, noise, frozen c, N, g) group of the freeze (8 reads: the core information-gain
# and CMI cells of one layout share a read where they froze at one c; the keep probe reads both
# keep arms; the atomic arm's two paths are two reads, each with both cuts); every call names
# the committed freeze (discover asserts its ancestry and its context mode) and stages on the
# s context test read of the same seed, grain and probe (`--prior-rung-record <ledger sha256>`).
# Inputs on the box (input_artifacts): input/m-latent-s4/model (the frozen backbone directory of
# the landed seed-4 Job V) and input/m-latent-s4/pretrain-run/results.json (the pretrain record
# annotate reads). One command per line; the runner's cwd is the harness directory; set -e stops
# at the first failure. Results land under results-context/ (never results/).
